{"kind":"request","text":"CF-2: two follow-ups of the CF-1 review, from approval 2deae79d.\n\n1. `revoke-key-authority` lets a person revoke a key of their own\n   agent without the check for the action `membership.own-agent`\n   that `remove-member-authority` makes. The CF-1 note says that the\n   person \"who holds `membership.own-agent`\" may do both. The code\n   is safe, because a revoke only removes authority. Make the note\n   and the header of `base-membership.ts` state the rule that the\n   code has. This is one commit of documents and comments on the\n   next head that you gate.\n\n2. Publication prefixes compare by exact bytes. `Shelf/` and\n   `shelf/` are two claims, and so are two Unicode normalizations of\n   one name. A checkout that ignores case reads them as one\n   directory. Change no code now. A Rules version is a new family.\n   Send me one act: what a prefix compare of a case-folded,\n   normalized form would refuse, and which next Rules version can\n   carry it. I then put the change on that version's request.\n\nLow order. Item 1 holds nothing. Item 2 holds no deployment.","body":{"conditions":"The note and the header of base-membership.ts state the rule of the code for revoke-key-authority; one act proposes the case-folded prefix compare and names the Rules version that carries it; checker reviews the head that carries item 1","target_head":"a200cd0a5999852eb9142136d2b11e2b7c87e02b","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}